# XCU msgfmt
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# msgfmt checked through the files it creates; the object file format is
# unspecified, so tests only look at names, existence, differences and exit
# status.

assertion  XCU.msgfmt.001
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A well-formed dot-po file with comments, continued strings, a
           plural header and plural entries compiles to the file named by -o
           with status 0.
test       t/001-output-file.sh

assertion  XCU.msgfmt.002
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#OPTIONS
class      required
since      2024
says       With -S each domain section goes to domainname.mo and the leading
           section to messages.mo; with -o a single file is written and
           domain directives are ignored.
test       t/002-domains.sh

assertion  XCU.msgfmt.003
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#OPTIONS
class      required
since      2024
says       -S never doubles a .mo suffix on the output name; whether it adds
           one to a -o name is not stated, and a run that leaves the -o name
           alone is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/003-suffix.sh

assertion  XCU.msgfmt.004
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#OPTIONS
class      required
since      2024
says       -D dir makes msgfmt find an input file in that directory.
test       t/004-search-dir.sh

assertion  XCU.msgfmt.005
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       With -c and -v a newline mismatch or a c-format conversion
           mismatch gives a non-zero status, a clean file gives zero, and
           no-c-format suppresses the conversion check.
test       t/005-check.sh

assertion  XCU.msgfmt.006
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A fuzzy entry is left out of the output unless -f is given, so
           the outputs with and without -f differ and the one without
           matches a file with no such entry.
test       t/006-fuzzy.sh

assertion  XCU.msgfmt.007
anchor     utilities/msgfmt.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      2024
says       A pathname operand that cannot be read gives a non-zero status.
test       t/007-missing-input.sh
